{"agent":"dedupe-t4-links","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The `answer` property claims to return \"the recorded dedupe answer of the NEWEST add that carried one\", and it computes `max(self.answers, key=lambda e: (self.answers[e].get(\"at\", \"\"), e))`. But the schema for `answers` is documented in this same dataclass as `{answer, score, candidates}` — note there is no `at` key. With that schema, `self.answers[e].get(\"at\", \"\")` is the empty string for every entry, so the key degenerates to `(\"\", e)` and the \"newest\" answer is actually whichever add event id is lexicographically largest. Given two additions (e.g. from two clones as the docstring itself anticipates), the answer returned is determined by event-id string order rather than by time, so if the add event ids do not happen to sort in reverse-chronological order the property returns a stale answer instead of the newest one. Either the stored schema must include `at` (and the population code must write it) or the selection must use the add event's timestamp.","digest":"06a1cdb894956ab3","location":"ddflow/core/model.py:RecordLinks.answer","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/model.py:RecordLinks.answer"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`link.recorded` is supposed to record \"later links *and* `distinct` dismissals\" (see the handler's own docstring and the stated acceptance). Dismissals arrive as `data = {\"relation\": \"distinct\", \"target\": <other id>}`, but the guard `if relation not in LINK_RELATIONS: return` only admits the add-time link relations (`extends`, `duplicate_of`, `related` — the exact three hard-coded in the `_linking` wrapper). `distinct` is a dismissal, not a link relation, so it is not in `LINK_RELATIONS`, and the handler returns before ever calling `_link`.\n\nConcrete failure: apply `Event(kind=\"link.recorded\", subject=\"BUG-1\", data={\"relation\": \"distinct\", \"target\": \"BUG-2\"})` after BUG-1 was added with `duplicate_of: [\"BUG-2\"]`. The dismissal produces no entry in `st.links[\"BUG-1\"].link_entries`, so a replay/consumer still sees BUG-1 as `duplicate_of` BUG-2 with no record that the user dismissed the pair. Had `distinct` been handled (separate branch or included in the admitted set), the dismissal would have been stored.","digest":"fde7c44ac6a5db84","location":"ddflow/core/model.py — `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/model.py — `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":20610,"diff_sha":"31aa1d1bcb46772128f181c4f4ad10a06accebce4b685b4feff115617c6070ce","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-link-events","elapsed_s":288.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/model.py:RecordLinks.answer","ddflow/core/model.py — `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e85fd6ed55d66ec9d9ffd3532","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":8082,"schema":1,"subject":"B-link-events","ts":"2026-10-02T06:09:35.587892Z"}
