{"agent":"dedupe-t4-links","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The `links` property sorts entries by `(x[\"at\"], x[\"event\"], x[\"target\"])`, but `link_entries` is keyed by event + relation + target, so `relation` is part of an entry's identity yet is omitted from the ordering key. If one event produces two link entries to the same target with different relations, the two sort keys collide and their relative order falls back to dict insertion order — i.e. to fold order. Concretely: an add event `E1` at time `t` that carries both `extends: [\"B\"]` and `related: [\"B\"]` yields entries `{\"event\":\"E1\",\"relation\":\"extends\",\"target\":\"B\",\"at\":\"t\"}` and `{\"event\":\"E1\",\"relation\":\"related\",\"target\":\"B\",\"at\":\"t\"}`; both have sort key `(\"t\",\"E1\",\"B\")`, so folding `E1` before vs. after an unrelated event (which changes insertion order) produces different `links` lists from the same event set. This contradicts the class's stated invariant (\"the fold is commutative ... in any order\") and makes `links` non-canonical. Note the `answer` property deliberately breaks ties with the event id, and `extensions` explicitly promises a fixed order, so this key looks like an omission; adding `x[\"relation\"]` to the key (e.g. `(x[\"at\"], x[\"event\"], x[\"target\"], x[\"relation\"])`) would make the order fold-independent.","digest":"2012e16286f9709c","location":"ddflow/core/model.py `RecordLinks.links`","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/core/model.py `RecordLinks.links`"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The handler's own docstring promises it handles \"a 'distinct' dismissal\", but the first thing it does is\n\n    relation = d.get(\"relation\", \"\")\n    if relation not in LINK_RELATIONS:\n        return\n\nso any `link.recorded` event whose relation is not in `LINK_RELATIONS` is silently discarded, with no state change and no error. `LINK_RELATIONS` is the record-link vocabulary for `extends` / `duplicate_of` / `related` — the same three names that the new `_linking` wrapper hardcodes a few lines above (it cannot use `LINK_RELATIONS` because that would then also expose `distinct` as an add-event link field). `distinct` is a dismissal, not one of those three link fields.\n\nConcrete input: a fold containing `{\"kind\": \"link.recorded\", \"subject\": \"B-1\", \"data\": {\"relation\": \"distinct\", \"target\": \"B-2\"}, \"by\": \"alice\", ...}`. Execution reaches the guard, `\"distinct\" not in LINK_RELATIONS` is true, and the function returns before `_link` is ever called, so `st.links[\"B-1\"].link_entries` never receives the `B-1:distinct:B-2` entry (and no `additions`/`answers` change either). A replay of the same log therefore rebuilds exactly the same state, and the earlier `duplicate_of B-2` link on B-1 remains the only recorded relation — the dismissal has no effect in any fold order, and the acceptance item \"link.recorded: later links and 'distinct' dismissals\" is not met for the dismissal case.","digest":"24c91b28bbe5a2e4","location":"ddflow/core/model.py `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/core/model.py `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":20614,"diff_sha":"e01a8afb9df34d014ae617ba90443ec975ae98f22864671238b6a07da259f917","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-link-events","elapsed_s":424.1,"family":"deepseek","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/model.py `RecordLinks.links`","ddflow/core/model.py `_h_link_recorded` (the `relation not in LINK_RELATIONS` guard)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"efb0287488685674d4865e7b3","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":8179,"schema":1,"subject":"B-link-events","ts":"2026-10-02T06:29:45.052838Z"}
