{"agent":"dedupe-t4-links","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The new helper evaluates `list | tuple` at call time:\n\n```python\ndef link_targets(v: Any) -> list[str]:\n    if isinstance(v, str):\n        return [v] if v else []\n    if isinstance(v, list | tuple):   # <-- union type used as isinstance second arg\n        return [x for x in v if isinstance(x, str) and x]\n    return []\n```\n\n`X | Y` produces a `types.UnionType` only on Python 3.10+. On 3.9 and earlier, `list | tuple` raises `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for |: 'type' and 'type'` — and crucially it is raised *before* `isinstance` even runs, so it fires on every invocation, not just when the value is a list/tuple. Because `_linking` calls `link_targets(d.get(relation))` for every relation in `ADD_RELATIONS` on every add event, a single `bug.found`, `task.added`, `phase.added`, `lesson.recorded`, etc. event will crash the fold on such an interpreter (and therefore also break replay). The rest of this same file is written in a 3.9-compatible style — it uses `dict[str, Callable[...]]` annotations and the sibling function even guards with the old-style `isinstance(d.get(\"dedupe\"), dict)` — so the module is evidently expected to run on interpreters below 3.10, where this construct is a hard runtime error. Concrete demonstration: under CPython 3.9, `fold([Event(kind=\"bug.found\", subject=\"B1\", ...)])` reaches `_linking.handle` → `link_targets(None)` → `list | tuple` → `TypeError`, aborting the fold instead of recording the link fields.","digest":"0f17d7f747910e46","location":"ddflow/core/model.py `link_targets` (`isinstance(v, list | tuple)`)","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/model.py `link_targets` (`isinstance(v, list | tuple)`)"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":23233,"diff_sha":"f1b480ae339e2ca8eb55090c3121eddad4692e169a9f754bead349bc0a4ea4b7","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-link-events","elapsed_s":670.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/core/model.py `link_targets` (`isinstance(v, list | tuple)`)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"ed7cd500e58243090797245db","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":8267,"schema":1,"subject":"B-link-events","ts":"2026-10-02T06:46:16.164965Z"}
